{title: Holy, Holy, Holy! Lord God Almighty}
{lyricist: Reginald Heber}
{composer: John B. Dykes}
{year: 1826}
{meta: tune-year 1861}
{key: D}
{time: 4/4}
{meta: tune NICAEA}
{meta: meter 11.12.12.10}
{meta: variation The hymn, sung to NICAEA}
{meta: license public-domain}
{meta: tags Trinity, holiness, morning}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]Holy, [Bm]holy, [G]holy! [D]Lord God Al[A]mighty!
[D]Early in the [Bm]morning our [E7]song shall rise to [A]Thee;
[D]Holy, [Bm]holy, [G]holy, [D]merciful and [A]mighty!
[Bm]God in three [G]Persons, [D]bless[A]ed Trini[D]ty!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D]Holy, [Bm]holy, [G]holy! [D]All the saints a[A]dore Thee,
[D]Casting down their [Bm]golden crowns a[E7]round the glassy [A]sea;
[D]Cherubim and [Bm]seraphim [G]falling [D]down be[A]fore Thee,
[Bm]Who wert, and [G]art, and [D]ever[A]more shalt [D]be.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[D]Holy, [Bm]holy, [G]holy! [D]Though the darkness [A]hide Thee,
[D]Though the eye of [Bm]sinful man Thy [E7]glory may not [A]see;
[D]Only [Bm]Thou art [G]holy; [D]there is none be[A]side Thee,
[Bm]Perfect in [G]power, in [D]love, [A]and puri[D]ty.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[D]Holy, [Bm]holy, [G]holy! [D]Lord God Al[A]mighty!
[D]All Thy works shall [Bm]praise Thy name, in [E7]earth, and sky, and [A]sea;
[D]Holy, [Bm]holy, [G]holy, [D]merciful and [A]mighty!
[Bm]God in three [G]Persons, [D]bless[A]ed Trini[D]ty!
{end_of_verse}
